  "description": "Dean's proposal, 2026-08-09: drop the top of the cost curve instead of adding an upgrade rule. Tier 1 costs 1-2 cards, Tier 2 costs 2-3, Tier 3 costs 3-4, and nothing in the game costs 5 or 6. Every Tier 2 and Tier 3 card is 3-of-suit plus wilds today, so the suit gate is left alone as the tier signature and the WILD component is what comes off: T2 3+0 -> 2+0 and 3+1 -> 3+0, T3 3+2 -> 3+0 and 3+3 -> 3+1. A6 The Garden Hive, the one 3-cost Tier 1, comes to 2. A PRICE arm, not a power arm: it tests whether affordability alone gets the upper tiers into play, and whether anything else moves when it does. ⛔ PASSENGERS PINNED 12/09/2026: Dean's plain-action balloon and Village Store ruling moved sixteen shipped leaves at once. This overlay predates that flip and every report taken against it does too, so each of those leaves is pinned here BY NAME at its PRE-FLIP value. Without it an arm read as a delta against a pre-flip base would silently gain a one-card flight, an always-present Aerodrome and a live coin economy. That is the 05/09/2026 passenger lesson: an overlay that should not move with the shipped default has to pin every knob the flip moved.",
